    <!-- Allah (الله) in square Kufic (kufi murabbaʿ). Original artwork: drawn
         on a 7×7 grid, one unit per stroke and one per gap, so no typeface
         is involved and no font licence applies. The initial alif is laid
         horizontally over the word, the standard squaring liberty of the
         script; lam and lam are the verticals, the final heh is the closed
         box, and the baseline joins heh to both lams.

         The same drawing as the launcher mark, stepped back by the same
         0.8576 ratio it stepped back on the launcher (1.34, owner decision),
         so the status bar and the launcher agree on how large the mark sits.
         This viewport is Material's 24-unit icon box, not the launcher's
         plate, so the two files carry different numbers for the same intent:
         here the ink is 0.715 of the box, where the launcher's is 0.352 of
         its canvas, and each platform frames it in its own plate. The path
         is the 108-unit geometry scaled into this viewport, not a redrawn
         copy, and the ink is centred on the box rather than the box's own
         centre, which a symmetric glyph hides but this one does not. -->
